1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,380
What stops two clicks on the pay button from charging the card twice?

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:07,309
Two confirms arrive at the same moment, and both try to debit.

3
00:00:07,309 --> 00:00:12,940
An atomic update moves the payment from open to authorizing, and only one caller can win it.

4
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:17,130
The winner resolves the terminal, and freezes the commission for this payment.

5
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:21,571
Every call to the processing center is written to an operation journal first.

6
00:00:21,571 --> 00:00:25,535
Then the adapter authorizes, which places a hold on the card.

7
00:00:25,535 --> 00:00:28,154
Then it captures, and the money really moves.

8
00:00:28,154 --> 00:00:33,535
On approval, the payment becomes captured, with the scheme's reference number, the RRN.

9
00:00:33,535 --> 00:00:39,178
A state machine allows only legal moves, so a captured payment can never go back to open.

10
00:00:39,178 --> 00:00:42,547
Next, seeing inside the system when something is slow.

